  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme for Country Partnership for Cuba (2026#2030)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Cuba, through its Ministry of Foreign Trade and Foreign Investments (MINCEX), formally requested UNIDO, in its letter of 9 April 2025 addressed to the Director General (attached), to support the development of a Programme for Country Partnership (PCP) in alignment with the National Plan for Economic and Social Development towards 2030 (PNDES 2030) and with the cooperation priorities identified in the United Nations Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework (UNSDCF) 2026-2030.  The letter acknowledges the positive results achieved jointly by UNIDO and the Government in the implementation of projects and, based on this experience, calls for advancing towards the formulation of the PCP 2026#2030. Prior to this formal request, during the visit of UNIDO#s Director General, Gerd M&#xfc;ller, to Havana in May 2024, the President of Cuba, Miguel D&#xed;az-Canel, expressed appreciation for UNIDO#s support to Cuba#s industrial development and requested the strengthening of UNIDO#s engagement in the country, including through the establishment of a permanent office.  The PCP will build on the successful, long-standing cooperation with Cuba and represents a strategic tool for achieving inclusive and sustainable industrial growth, while addressing the country#s economic and environmental challenges. The PCP will</narrative>
  </description>
